  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding from Alaska Medicaid Zulresso Criteria Version 1; Original: 2/8/2022; Approval: 4/15/2022; Effective: 6/1/2022. The archived extraction artifact raft is retained only as the pack slug; the drug is Zulresso (brexanolone).",
    "Encoded: closed postpartum_depression indication, age ≥18, all nine approval requirements and active psychosis/breastfeeding denials. Clinical requirements use attestations; verify supporting documentation. The oral antidepressant trial must be at maximally indicated dose for at least 6–8 weeks; the alternative requires contraindication or intolerance to at least two antidepressants from two different classes. Failure to meet approval criteria is represented by approval predicates.",
    "Cautions (notes only): monitor for excessive sedation and sudden loss of consciousness; monitor for hypoxia using pulse oximetry; use with caution in end stage renal disease (ESRD); monitor for suicidal thoughts and behaviors. These cautions require manual review and are not additional denial predicates.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval is one 60-hour infusion.",
    "Quantity (notes only): weight-based dosing not to exceed a 60-hour infusion; HCPCS J1632. Duration and quantity enforcement require manual review.",
    "Zurzuvae is a PPD peer alternative; eligibility is evaluated separately under its own criteria."
  ],
